Cannot authenticate into mongo, &quot;auth fails&quot;
Authenticating with MongoDB MongoDB is a document-oriented, open source database. It is designed to provide high performance, scalability, and flexibility while minimizing the amount of effort needed to set up and maintain the database. When using MongoDB, it is important to ensure that authentication is enabled. This will ensure that only authorized users have access to the database.
Creating an Admin User To authenticate into MongoDB, the first step is to create an admin user.

What's the difference between Spring Data's MongoTemplate and MongoRepository? What&rsquo;s the Difference Between Spring Data&rsquo;s MongoTemplate and MongoRepository?
When writing an application that requires complex queries using spring-data and mongodb, it can be difficult to use MongoRepository due to a lack of examples of complex queries or understanding of the syntax. Queries such as the following require a deep understanding of the syntax:
@Repository public interface UserRepositoryInterface extends MongoRepository { List findByEmailOrLastName(String email, String lastName); } Or the use of JSON based queries which can be difficult to understand and get the syntax right.
